<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Tsunami</h1>
<p>Sphere: Summoning Sphere
Class: Druid (guild level 52)
Mana: 50
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre><a cmd='#'>cast tsunami</a>
</pre>
<p>The druid raises both arms, screams 'Maelestra Aquaris!' and summons a 
tidal wave that washes everything in the room away through one open exit, 
chosen at random (never up or down). Everyone goes with it, the caster too, 
and so do all the things that can be picked up. Those inside a boat go 
with their boat.
</p><p>It only works on water you swim or sail on; anywhere else, or when no exit 
is open, nothing happens. It isn't an attack, so it starts no fight: a 
druid can use it to sweep an enemy away, or to get away. You must be 
standing.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Summoning Sphere</a>
</pre>




</div>